        // (x, y), (x, -y), (-x, y), (-x, -y)
        // We need to find integers a, b, c, d such that:
        // a*(x,y) + b*(x,-y) + c*(-x,y) + d*(-x,-y) = (dx, dy)
        // This simplifies to:
        // (a + b - c - d) * x = dx
        // (a - b + c - d) * y = dy
        // Let u = a + b - c - d, v = a - b + c - d
        // Then u * x = dx and v * y = dy
        // So dx must be divisible by x and dy must be divisible by y
        // But we also need to check if there exist integers a,b,c,d satisfying the system.
        // From the equations:
        // a + b - c - d = dx/x (if x divides dx)
        // a - b + c - d = dy/y (if y divides dy)
        // Let p = dx/x, q = dy/y (these must be integers)
        // Then we need:
        // a + b - c - d = p
        // a - b + c - d = q
        // Adding: 2a - 2d = p + q => a - d = (p+q)/2
        // Subtracting: 2b - 2c = p - q => b - c = (p-q)/2
        // So (p+q) must be even and (p-q) must be even, i.e., p and q must have the same parity.

        if (x == 0 || y == 0) {
            // But x, y >= 1 per constraints, so this won't happen
